### Pulse — Slice 2 HTTP tests
### Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
### Set @token variables after login by copying the token from the response.
###
### Pre-requisites:
###   - npm run dev (server running on port 5000)
###   - npm run seed:admin (admin account created)
###   - Database rebuilt with 00–02 + 20_audit_notifications.sql

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### ── Variables (fill in after running the login requests below) ──────────────
@donorToken  = PASTE_DONOR_TOKEN_HERE
@staffToken  = PASTE_STAFF_TOKEN_HERE
@adminToken  = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE

# =============================================================================
# PHASE B1 — Auth & hospitals
# =============================================================================

### T_HEALTH — Server health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

###

### T5 — Signup as donor (first time)
# @name signupDonor
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "DONOR",
  "name": "Test Donor",
  "email": "testdonor@test.com",
  "password": "Test@123",
  "phone": "9000000001",
  "blood_type": "A+"
}

###

### T5 — Duplicate email → 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "DONOR",
  "name": "Test Donor Again",
  "email": "testdonor@test.com",
  "password": "Test@123",
  "phone": "9000000001",
  "blood_type": "A+"
}

###

### Login as seeded donor (Aarav)
# @name loginAarav
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "DONOR",
  "email": "aarav@example.com",
  "password": "Pulse@123"
}

###

### Login as seeded staff (City Care — verified hospital)
# @name loginStaff
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "STAFF",
  "email": "staff.citycare@example.com",
  "password": "Pulse@123"
}

###

### Login as admin (created by seed:admin)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "email": "admin@pulse.test",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}

###

### T6 — Wrong password → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "DONOR",
  "email": "aarav@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

###

### T6 — Unknown email → 401 (SAME message as wrong password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "DONOR",
  "email": "nobody@nowhere.com",
  "password": "Pulse@123"
}

###

### T7 — No token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

###

### GET /auth/me with valid token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{donorToken}}

###

### Public hospital list (no auth needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/hospitals

###

# =============================================================================
# PHASE B3 — Admin routes
# =============================================================================

### T11 — Donor calling /admin/stats → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{donorToken}}

###

### T11 — Staff calling /admin/stats → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

###

### Admin stats (should return 200 with counts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### Admin user list
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### Admin audit log
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### Admin notification queue health
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### Verify hospital 4 (New Hope — seeded as unverified)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/hospitals/4/verify
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "verified": true
}

###

### Unverify hospital 4 again
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/hospitals/4/verify
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "verified": false
}

###

### T10 — Staff of unverified hospital (New Hope) should get 403 on /requests
### (requires Member A's routes/requests.js to be merged)
### Login first as staff.newhope@example.com, use that token here.
# POST {{baseUrl}}/requests
# Authorization: Bearer NEWHOPE_STAFF_TOKEN_HERE
# Content-Type: application/json
# { "request_type": "BLOOD", "blood_type_needed": "O+", "urgency": "MODERATE" }

###

### T12 — Deactivate donor 1 (Aarav), then try to log in
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/donor/1/active
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "is_active": false
}

###

### T12 — Deactivated donor login attempt → 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "DONOR",
  "email": "aarav@example.com",
  "password": "Pulse@123"
}

###

### Reactivate donor 1 after the test
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/donor/1/active
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "is_active": true
}

###

### Run eligibility restore job manually
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/jobs/restore-eligibility
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

# =============================================================================
# Notifications (donor)
# =============================================================================

### GET /notifications/me (donor)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/me
Authorization: Bearer {{donorToken}}

###

### Non-donor (staff) trying /notifications/me → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/me
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

###

### T8 — Donor calling POST /requests → 403
### (uncomment once Member A's routes/requests.js is merged)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/requests
# Authorization: Bearer {{donorToken}}
# Content-Type: application/json
# { "request_type": "BLOOD", "blood_type_needed": "O+", "urgency": "CRITICAL" }
